## RTK Command Shape

When running `go test`, `go build`, or `golangci-lint run` in an RTK-enabled shell, the executable must be the first top-level token so RTK can intercept it.

- Do not prefix these commands with inline environment variable assignments.
- Do not wrap these commands in shell command substitution.
- Do not use `make` for these commands when a direct top-level command is available.
- If a workflow would normally use `make`, run the underlying RTK-compatible command instead.
- Set required environment variables in separate commands first, then run the bare command.

Good:

```bash
export KUBEBUILDER_ASSETS="$(pwd)/$(./bin/setup-envtest use 1.32.0 --bin-dir ./bin -p path)"
export FLEET_CLUSTER_WATCH_NAMESPACE="kube-system"
go test ./...
```

Bad:

```bash
KUBEBUILDER_ASSETS="$(pwd)/$(./bin/setup-envtest use 1.32.0 --bin-dir ./bin -p path)" go test ./...
make test
make lint
make build
```
